Description: Apple T2 bridge driver (BCE, VHCI, audio) as a DKMS module
 The driver for the T2 security chip's Buffer Copy Engine in Intel Macs
 from 2018 on: the virtual USB host controller behind the internal
 keyboard, trackpad, Touch Bar and camera, and the T2 audio interface.
 Without it a T2 Mac has no internal keyboard under Linux. Built from the
 t2linux project's apple-bce-drv (the aur branch, which suspends and
 resumes) for every installed kernel by DKMS. Part of the MaluOS apple-t2
 component; the installer adds it on a T2 Mac.
